Architecture review of chunk c3 complete. Wrote 1 finding to `architecture-c3.json`.

**Summary of what I verified:**

- **form_copy.gleam** (343 lines) — clean leaf module following the `application/form_copy.gleam` precedent; all em-dashes found are in comments only (lines 3, 7, 20, 198, 336), never in user-facing copy strings — no ban violation.
- **form_pages.gleam** (382 lines) — within the 400-line view target; `page_shell` properly private; brand header/footer reused from `application/form_view` (sanctioned by spec + r1 W10); head intentionally diverges from apply form (AC7: no PostHog/consent).
- **form_question_pages.gleam** (441 lines) — marginally over 400 but the spec anticipated/performsd the split; clean dependency DAG (form_copy ← questions ← form_question_pages).
- **SQL queries** — all four new queries (`get_form_context_by_form_token`, `stamp_form_opened`, `save_draft_answer`, `remint_form_token`, `restore_form_token`) follow the existing `get_reference_call_by_form_token` COALESCE/NULLIF conventions; guards consistent with A7 (taken-over rows still save/stamp; remint/restore exclude taken-over).

**The one finding** (note): the resend POST form is duplicated verbatim between `view_expired` and `view_resend_failed` — a clear DRY opportunity per AGENTS.md's own "extract helpers when logic repeats 2+ places" rule.

Rejected as too weak: the `view_options`/`view_options_named` single-caller wrapper, the `prefill_value` naming across modules (disambiguated by module prefix, shared predicate prevents drift), and the parallel `AsStatedText` branching in view vs validator (both delegate to the same `questions.prefill_value`).
